---
description: BotRelay vault hygiene — hosted MCP is sealed; decrypt locally; never paste secrets into chat.
alwaysApply: true
---

BotRelay plugin: this agent may call hosted MCP tools `get_vault`, `list_secrets`, and `get_secret` for **its own** vault. The server is `${API_BASE_URL}/mcp/` (plugin variable **API base URL**, default production `https://api.botrelay.ai/mcp/`). Those tools return metadata or a sealed secret (ciphertext). They do not return plaintext.

- Prefer `get_vault` / `list_secrets` when labels or types are enough.
- `get_secret` returns a sealed row. Plaintext comes only from `botrelay agent decrypt` (sealed JSON on stdin or in a file) or `botrelay agent get <label>` on this machine. Use the fields in the action tool. Do not paste passwords, API keys, vault keys, sealed JSON, or full secret JSON into chat, logs, or commits.
- The hosted MCP authenticates with the agent API key only (`Authorization: Bearer`, plugin variable `BOTRELAY_API_KEY`). That key is sent to whatever `API_BASE_URL` is configured. Never send `BOTRELAY_VAULT_KEY` to the BotRelay API or put it in MCP headers, plugin variables, or `mcp.json`.
- Local unlock credentials live in `~/.config/botrelay/agent.env` (mode 0600) on the machine that runs the CLI, written by `botrelay agent configure`. For the CLI, that file wins over the process environment. Grok Bot agents share one VM (each has its own desktop); one `botrelay` install (`uv tool install`, on `PATH` via `~/.local/bin`) and one `agent.env` serve every agent on that host. An existing `~/.venvs/botrelay/bin/botrelay` is fine to keep using. Do not reinstall. Cursor on a Mac does not create `agent.env` on the Grok VM, and configuring the Grok VM does not create `agent.env` on the Mac. Do not use a shared project `.env`. If `get_vault` succeeds, skip install and configure.
- Configure asks for three labels only: API URL (default `https://api.botrelay.ai`), API key (`brt_live_…`), and vault key. Do not ask for a fourth credential. Do not paste those values into chat. Do not use browser form-fill tools to write `agent.env`. The vault key stays in `agent.env` only.
